nd CMOs; and","context":"●experience delays in our preclinical studies, clinical trials or regulatory approval for our current or any future product candidates, including with respect to failed studies, inconclusive results, safety issues or other regulatory challenges;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":806,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-027964","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-16","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001953926","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1953926/000110465926027964/zbio-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/1b8cbda836e0253ed9edab6fd3cda667e19d071a926ee9ef83e05100e3c15c2c.bin","sha256":"1b8cbda836e0253ed9edab6fd3cda667e19d071a926ee9ef83e05100e3c15c2c"}},{"id":"47100e974eff98f50fe9d16fdc556bbc469582561b2e5c1041bdc3273bf3a58b","quote":"●incur additional costs associated with being a public company, including audit, legal, regulatory and tax-related services associated with maintaining compliance with an exchange listing and the Securities and Exchange Commission (the “SEC”) requirements, director and officer insurance premiums and investor relations costs.","context":"●establish agreements with CROs and CMOs; and","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":807,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-027964","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-16","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001953926","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1953926/000110465926027964/zbio-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/1b8cbda836e0253ed9edab6fd3cda667e19d071a926ee9ef83e05100e3c15c2c.bin","sha256":"1b8cbda836e0253ed9edab6fd3cda667e19d071a926ee9ef83e05100e3c15c2c"}},{"id":"938a25dd00f7a950ebf54267fd409b89a73b870ae328d39bccfd621366b1979a","quote":"Even if we succeed in commercializing one or more product candidates, we expect to incur substantial expenditures to develop and market additional product candidates.","context":"●incur additional costs associated with being a public company, including audit, legal, regulatory and tax-related services associated with maintaining compliance with an exchange listing and the Securities and Exchange Commission (the “SEC”) requirements, director and officer insurance premiums and investor relations costs.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":808,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-027964","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-16","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001953926","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1953926/000110465926027964/zbio-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/1b8cbda836e0253ed9edab6fd3cda667e19d071a926ee9ef83e05100e3c15c2c.bin","sha256":"1b8cbda836e0253ed9edab6fd3cda667e19d071a926ee9ef83e05100e3c15c2c"}},{"id":"27411ead90ef67c54ee42a568f21c24ea1454bc9fb3f3d7705b45639162f529c","quote":"We will require substantial additional financing to achieve our goals, and failure to obtain additional capital when needed, or on acceptable terms, would cause us to delay, limit, reduce or terminate our product development efforts.","context":"Even if we succeed in commercializing one or more product candidates, we expect to incur substantial expenditures to develop and market additional product candidates.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":809,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-027964","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-16","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001953926","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1953926/000110465926027964/zbio-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/1b8cbda836e0253ed9edab6fd3cda667e19d071a926ee9ef83e05100e3c15c2c.bin","sha256":"1b8cbda836e0253ed9edab6fd3cda667e19d071a926ee9ef83e05100e3c15c2c"}},{"id":"f8d16cb079c5dfb86c8c38ede24a5cf2abaab3356dbc5442088529cd2ffa4ded","quote":"The development of biopharmaceutical product candidates, including conducting preclinical studies and clinical trials, is a time consuming, capital-intensive and uncertain process. Our operations have consumed substantial amounts of cash since inception. We expect our expenses to substantially increase in connection with our ongoing and future activities, including, without limitation, our two Phase 3 trials of orelabrutinib in forms of progressive MS. If we obtain regulatory approval for obexelimab or other product candidates, we also expect to incur significant commercialization expenses related to manufacturing, marketing, sales and distribution of such products, and we will incur costs as part of pre-commercialization preparations for a potential launch of obexelimab. In addition, other unanticipated costs may arise. Because the outcome of any clinical trial or preclinical study is uncertain, we cannot reliably estimate the actual amount of capital necessary to successfully complete the development and commercialization of obexelimab, orelabrutinib and other product candidates.","context":"We will require substantial additional financing to achieve our goals, and failure to obtain additional capital when needed, or on acceptable terms, would cause us to delay, limit, reduce or terminate our product development efforts.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":810,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-027964","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-16","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001953926","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1953926/000110465926027964/zbio-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/1b8cbda836e0253ed9edab6fd3cda667e19d071a926ee9ef83e05100e3c15c2c.bin","sha256":"1b8cbda836e0253ed9edab6fd3cda667e19d071a926ee9ef83e05100e3c15c2c"}},{"id":"43e91b2f89a5d855c5eba21723fb8f22ea30963099f8d7e2e33280652fd59afd","quote":"As of December 31, 2025, we had $360.5 million in cash, cash equivalents and investments. Based on our current operating plans, we expect that our existing cash, cash equivalents and investments together with the $71.5 million of net proceeds received to date in the first quarter of 2026 from sales under our ATM Program and the first tranche of $75.0 million available under the Company’s debt arrangement with Pharmakon (see Note 18, Subsequent Events, to our consolidated financial statements included elsewhere in this Annual Report), will be sufficient to fund our operations and capital expenditure requirements for approximately twelve months from the date of our consolidated financial statements are issued. However, due to the uncertainties inherent in forecasting our future cash requirements, management has concluded that these resources are not sufficient to alleviate substantial doubt with respect to our ability to continue as a going concern. Our financial statements do not include any adjustments or changes in classification of assets or liabilities that may result from our possible inability to continue as a going concern. However, we expect to finance our operations through private or public equity financing, debt financing or other capital resources.","context":"The development of biopharmaceutical product candidates, including conducting preclinical studies and clinical trials, is a time consuming, capital-intensive and uncertain process. Our operations have consumed substantial amounts of cash since inception. We expect our expenses to substantially increase in connection with our ongoing and future activities, including, without limitation, our two Phase 3 trials of orelabrutinib in forms of progressive MS. If we obtain regulatory approval for obexelimab or other product candidates, we also expect to incur significant commercialization expenses related to manufacturing, marketing, sales and distribution of such products, and we will incur costs as part of pre-commercialization preparations for a potential launch of obexelimab. In addition, other unanticipated costs may arise. Because the outcome of any clinical trial or preclinical study is uncertain, we cannot reliably estimate the actual amount of capital necessary to successfully complete the development and commercialization of obexelimab, orelabrutinib and other product candidates.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":811,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-027964","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-16","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001953926","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1953926/000110465926027964/zbio-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/1b8cbda836e0253ed9edab6fd3cda667e19d071a926ee9ef83e05100e3c15c2c.bin","sha256":"1b8cbda836e0253ed9edab6fd3cda667e19d071a926ee9ef83e05100e3c15c2c"}},{"id":"51376cfe2f8584c73b5dca70e9a59e6c2df0c3dd507bab72bc1af696073cfcbc","quote":"We will not generate revenue from product sales unless and until we successfully complete clinical development and obtain regulatory approval for a product candidate, and we may not ever generate significant revenue or profits. In addition, we expect to incur costs associated with operating as a public company, including significant legal, accounting, investor relations, and other expenses that we did not incur prior to our IPO. If we obtain regulatory approval for a product candidate and do not enter into a third-party commercialization partnership, we expect to incur significant expenses related to developing our commercialization capability to support product sales, marketing, manufacturing and distribution activities. We may also require additional capital to pursue in-licenses or acquisitions of other product candidates. As a result, we expect to incur substantial operating losses and negative operating cash flows for the foreseeable future.","context":"vestments. Based on our current operating plans, we expect that our existing cash, cash equivalents and investments together with the $71.5 million of net proceeds received to date in the first quarter of 2026 from sales under our ATM Program and the first tranche of $75.0 million available under the Company’s debt arrangement with Pharmakon (see Note 18, Subsequent Events, to our consolidated financial statements included elsewhere in this Annual Report), will be sufficient to fund our operations and capital expenditure requirements for approximately twelve months from the date of our consolidated financial statements are issued. However, due to the uncertainties inherent in forecasting our future cash requirements, management has concluded that these resources are not sufficient to alleviate substantial doubt with respect to our ability to continue as a going concern. Our financial statements do not include any adjustments or changes in classification of assets or liabilities that may result from our possible inability to continue as a going concern. However, we expect to finance our operations through private or public equity financing, debt financing or other capital resources.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":812,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-027964","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-16","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001953926","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1953926/000110465926027964/zbio-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/1b8cbda836e0253ed9edab6fd3cda667e19d071a926ee9ef83e05100e3c15c2c.bin","sha256":"1b8cbda836e0253ed9edab6fd3cda667e19d071a926ee9ef83e05100e3c15c2c"}},{"id":"7d05063f6ad091b6024de8d8b5f5b9baf0184a30ab67875460c0dd019d0f1a81","quote":"Because of the numerous risks and uncertainties associated with research, development and commercialization of product 